Add converter for legacy Gingko Desktop 2.x .gko archives

Purpose:
Let users of the old Gingko Desktop 2.x open their .gko files in the
new desktop app.

Approach:
- Old .gko files are 7z archives containing a PouchDB/leveldb database
  of git-like commit/tree/ref objects. On open, detect the 7z signature
  and offer conversion.
- Extract with sevenz-rust2, read the leveldb with rusty-leveldb, walk
  the head commit's tree, and emit <gingko-card> markdown (mirroring
  Coders.treeToMarkdownOutline).
- Unit test against a sanitized 2.x archive (client/tests/historic/).

Constraints:
- Never modify the original file: the converted document opens as a new
  Untitled document.
- Current-format .gko/.gkw files take the normal open path.

